"""The Front Burner's self-checks and session block (plan 2026-10-31, Phases 1-2).

dates   every active row (touched or not): overdue charter steps, rows with no open dated step
        and no `no_hard_date` record (A2), and `no_hard_date` records older than 30 days.
drift   activity vs. the board, per project, from git commit days plus the landed ledger.
        `quiet` needs positive evidence: a successful `git log` AND `git status`. The ledger
        keeps one entry per path (landed.merge), so it can prove activity, never its absence.
decide  records one closeout answer the same way every time, so the question does not repeat.
today   the session-start block: at most 15 lines (Phase 2, step 8).

dates and drift only report (Product Principle 4); `decide` changes the registry only on an
answer from Eric. Closeout Step 0 asks every `needs_eric` item in its one question batch.
